# Architecture

- Prefer the simplest solution that works; optimize only when asked
- One module / function = one reason to change (SRP)
- Depend on interfaces/abstractions, not concrete internals
- Keep business logic free of framework/UI/DB details
- Inject dependencies so units are easy to mock and test
- Prefer pure functions; treat hard-to-test code as a design smell
- Extract shared utilities only when a real pattern repeats (high fan-in)---
